  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This scholarly book is already showing signs of active use: it has 877 recorded downloads and is openly available in hybrid form, which supports broad access beyond the purchase market. The record also points to policy and civic relevance through its alignment with Peace, Justice and strong institutions, while the book received support from KU Leuven.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Ernst Wolff\u2019s Martin Versfeld brings renewed attention to one of South Africa\u2019s major philosophers, presenting his thought at the intersection of modernity, economic justice, simplicity, and environmental ethics. The book\u2019s profile suggests particular resonance for readers working across philosophy, theology, political thought, and sustainability-oriented scholarship, matching Versfeld\u2019s own concern with the moral costs of violent modernity and with ethical alternatives grounded in generosity and restraint.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The strongest measurable sign of impact is usage: the book has been downloaded 877 times, indicating sustained interest from readers. Its hybrid open-access status further extends reach by making at least part of the work freely available, and the repository record shows multiple open instances. This kind of access matters for a book whose subject matter speaks not only to specialists but also to broader audiences interested in ethics, justice, and ecological thought.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The surrounding evidence points more to emerging influence than to settled scholarly accumulation. OpenAlex currently records no citations, so the book\u2019s longer-term citation impact is not yet established in the available record. That said, the absence of citations should be read cautiously: for a 2021 scholarly book, the record can still be early, and the current signals of download activity, open availability, and thematic relevance already indicate that the work is being encountered and used.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Additional context reinforces the book\u2019s scholarly positioning. The publisher and funding record show institutional backing, and the subject alignment with peace, justice, and strong institutions suggests relevance to debates that extend beyond textual interpretation into public ethics and social critique. Taken together, the evidence portrays a book with clear conceptual range and a meaningful early readership, especially in areas where philosophy meets social and environmental responsibility.</p>",
